{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now","id":1173152,"title":"Ratkin Uprising: Apocalypse Now","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-03T20:35:41-08:00","id":1173152,"title":"Ratkin Uprising: Apocalypse Now","content":"So, the Ratkin are absurdly numerous these days compared to other changing breeds and supernaturals with nest of hundreds under major cities, with some nests approaching a thousand under the largest megacities like New York. <br /> <br /> Has anyone ever played a game where the Ratkin actually unleashed their plagues on humanity and rose up to paint the streets with the blood of the survivors (actual goal to sow chaos, massacre health care professionals, decapitate leadership and inhibit any coordinated response by human governments). How did it go?<br /> <br /> Simultaneous outbreak of Spanish Flu, Smallpox and Pneumonic Plague in cities across the world would likely kill at bare minimum a third of the world population and kill who knows how many else indirectly as the over worked health care system can't deal with normal issues. The economy would collapse, trade would grind to a halt, famine would break out over much of the world, secondary disease outbreaks would occur, anarchy and warfare would spread. And of course, a hundred thousand plus Ratkin rising up would inevitably reveal the existence of the supernatural to the mortal population.<br /> <br /> How would the Garou and other Changing Breeds respond to this?<br /> <br /> If a crossover with Mage, how would the Technocracy respond? If a crossover with Vampire, how would the Camarilla and the Sabbat react?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T21:23:29-08:00","id":1173157,"title":"","content":"Little confusion, you may be conflating Ratkin with all their family. Because Ratkin are only absurdly numerous in the sense their entire world population is comparable to all the Garou or all the Anansi. So you aren't really going to have more then say around 20k Ratkin on the high end, or 14k on the medium end.<br /> <br /> But that is enough to cause an insane Apocalypse. This would work best if they organize and enact a plan while say the Garou Nation are distracted. This is the type of thing the Nagah after all watch out for, same with Corax. But they know they are probably going to attract attention from all others, and there will likely be Banes and such that rise to Incarna status with an end of the world Plague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T00:59:53-08:00","id":1173173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1173157#post1173157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Little confusion, you may be conflating Ratkin with all their family. Because Ratkin are only absurdly numerous in the sense their entire world population is comparable to all the Garou or all the Anansi. So you aren't really going to have more then say around 20k Ratkin on the high end, or 14k on the medium end.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like there are a lot more than 20k, albeit not in the 100k neighborhood as I said originally.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Ratkin\u2019s massive breeding program has created<i><b> tens of thousands of new rodens Kinfolk, most of which have been exposed to the Birthing Plague</b></i>. The result was a massive population explosion ... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T02:27:15-08:00","id":1173183,"title":"","content":"The Birthing Plague kills a helluva lot more kin then it turns into Ratkin. But its fair to say W20 is supporting a new population boom of the Ratkin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T09:15:46-08:00","id":1173238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1173183#post1173183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Birthing Plague kills a helluva lot more kin then it turns into Ratkin. But its fair to say W20 is supporting a new population boom of the Ratkin.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were stated as being higher in number for a while before W20. It goes back to the breed book, where they had not just material recruits, but ones from the Umbra as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T01:01:37-08:00","id":1173435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1173157#post1173157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that is enough to cause an insane Apocalypse. This would work best if they organize and enact a plan while say the Garou Nation are distracted. This is the type of thing the Nagah after all watch out for, same with Corax. But they know they are probably going to attract attention from all others, and there will likely be Banes and such that rise to Incarna status with an end of the world Plague.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've managed to hide their huge growth in numbers, which one would think would be a lot more noticeable than a plan to unleash disease.<br /> <br /> How are the Nagah going to stop a grand international Ratkin conspiracy even if they uncover one? They can't assassinate their way out of this one. They'd have to get the garou on board, and I don't think they'd think of that before it was to late.<br /> <br /> As for the Corax, they like to get into everyone's business, but how much spying underground do they do? The Ratkin aren't going to be putting their doomsday plan on the internet or chat about it at the club or whatever where someone not a Ratkin could over hear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":".  Grammar 01-05-2018, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T13:31:10-08:00","id":1173562,"title":"","content":"The only reason to have absurdly large numbers of Ratkin is in chronicles where the Apocalypse is imminent or will take place. That is what the Revised era was about. If people aren't interested in a chronicle about that, the number of Ratkin should be substantially reduced. Although the ST might want there to be a rising population of Ratkin to indicate that his chronicle is set in the era where the Apocalypse is set to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T16:07:28-08:00","id":1173608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1173562#post1173562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reason to have absurdly large numbers of Ratkin is in chronicles where the Apocalypse is imminent or will take place. That is what the Revised era was about. If people aren't interested in a chronicle about that, the number of Ratkin should be substantially reduced. Although the ST might want there to be a rising population of Ratkin to indicate that his chronicle is set in the era where the Apocalypse is set to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, but that's what the thread is about, having an apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T18:20:04-08:00","id":1173652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1173608#post1173608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yes, but that's what the thread is about, having an apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just one? The sum of Ratkin, altogether, likely believe in (causing) about as many different apocalypses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T23:19:30-08:00","id":1173701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1173652#post1173652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just one? The sum of Ratkin, altogether, likely believe in (causing) about as many different apocalypses.</div> </div> </div> </div>They only need one to achieve their goal. And unleash the plagues is their signature doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T12:12:54-08:00","id":1173809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1173701#post1173701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They only need one to achieve their goal. And unleash the plagues is their signature doom.</div> </div> </div> </div>They used to have grades of response to human overpopulation. The opening salvo was typically &quot;eat the excess food&quot;, though in a modern context, that would probably extend to money and other facets of general economics.<br /> <br /> (With their tall tale powers, Munchmausen could probably bluff their way past any amount of security and convince corporate executives and bureaucrats to crash their own companies out of panic.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-06-2018, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T20:42:50-08:00","id":1173919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1173809#post1173809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They used to have grades of response to human overpopulation. The opening salvo was typically &quot;eat the excess food&quot;, though in a modern context, that would probably extend to money and other facets of general economics.<br /> <br /> (With their tall tale powers, Munchmausen could probably bluff their way past any amount of security and convince corporate executives and bureaucrats to crash their own companies out of panic.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a pretty amusing scene, but aren't Ratkin way too crazy to consider something that relatively complex and abstract?<br /> <br /> And really, why bother when the panic from a global pandemic will crash the economy and achieve the number one goal of population reduction at the same time.<br /> <br /> Manipulating the economy by itself will atract attention they don't want, while not achieving the desired megadeaths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T20:47:58-08:00","id":1173922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1173919#post1173919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like a pretty amusing scene, but aren't Ratkin way too crazy to consider something that relatively complex and abstract?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It's just going to get weird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And really, why bother when the panic from a global pandemic will crash the economy and achieve the number one goal of population reduction at the same time. </div> </div> </div>Style. Narrative roles. Expertise in it rather than biological warfare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Manipulating the economy by itself will atract attention they don't want, while not achieving the desired megadeaths. </div> </div> </div>Moon Mice are all about overly grandiose drama.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T23:42:05-08:00","id":1173974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1173922#post1173922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Style. Narrative roles. Expertise in it rather than biological warfare.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but the point of this thread was:<br /> <br /> The Ratkin have unleashed pandemics on humanity and have swarmed out of their sewers to attack hospitals and governments. How do the garou and other fera react? How about the Technocracy? How about the Camariila and Sabbat? <br /> <br /> No one has really answered that. I guess they all just give up, accept it as a fate accompli and barricade themsleves in their lairs in an attempt to ride out the apocalypse and rebuild on the ruins once its run its course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T12:49:25-08:00","id":1174113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1173974#post1173974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, but the point of this thread was:<br /> <br /> The Ratkin have unleashed pandemics on humanity and have swarmed out of their sewers to attack hospitals and governments. How do the garou and other fera react? How about the Technocracy? How about the Camariila and Sabbat?<br /> <br /> No one has really answered that. I guess they all just give up, accept it as a fate accompli and barricade themsleves in their lairs in an attempt to ride out the apocalypse and rebuild on the ruins once its run its course.</div> </div> </div> </div>(If they're going on disease-spreading sprees, they're far more likely to be quiet about it until the incubation periods are up.)<br /> <br /> I'm assuming that we're supposed to assume that all the other organizations exist? Hmph.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy would not be able to keep up as easily as they're presented as, for the same reason that they can't react very well to anything in Werewolf, they're not operating with very open eyes when it comes to anything from the Umbra, and even when they do have DiSci, their assumptions make them Wrong Genre Savvy about what's going on. This is particularly true if the Ratkin start spreading diseases that rats don't usually spread, like Ebola. The Progenitors could probably patch a lot of flare-ups, but they'd be running in circles if they did, and that would entail diverting funding from their shady bioweapons research, as well as leave them overextended against the Traditions, so they probably wouldn't max out their efforts. By the time they realize that they should have and that the Traditions are small potatoes in this scenario, they won't have the capacity to manage it. If any part of the Technocracy survives, expect them to make an instructional film entitled &quot;When Artificial Scarcity is Not Your Friend!&quot;<br /> <br /> Iteration X might not be affected by diseases to the same extent, but they do rely on infrastructure that Ratkin will probably chew through and set on fire. &quot;They cut the power&quot;, and &quot;That's inside the room!&quot; ensue, with a side of bricking everything computerized. ItX does not do well against enemies that can look at computers and brick them; even countermagick is not likely to help, since the rats will be rolling about twice as many dice for their bricking powers at half the difficulty, likely while firing old surplus support weapons and AKs at their targets.<br /> <br /> Also, Death Ray!<br /> <br /> Kindred of all bents will likely find their hunting capacity compromised and end up killing their own to thin their herds, either directly or as sacrifices in suicide missions. Some vampires who were feeding indiscriminately might also be carriers of deadly diseases; those would probably be cut first, where they become known. Expect blackmail of this variety to be the hot new thing in Cam backstabbing circles.<br /> <br /> The Beast Courts will probably be caught in a huge &quot;What the hell Nezumi?&quot; moment. That could potentially touch off another powder keg, assuming that the courts don't fine sufficient venting against everything else that tries to drag itself out of the shadows. Punishment of any instigators would probably have to focus on a few key conspirators as scapegoats, lest the most populous breed not be around to help with their court duties when everything starts going out of control. Suicide missions might be the atonement of choice, as getting together for the Rite of Hell Made Flesh is quite time-consuming, and as the Nezumi would likely point out, this does knock the Kumo down quite a few pegs, since they no longer have vast stores of blood to freely drink, much as with the vampires.<br /> <br /> The Shih are quite hardy, and will likely survive. They probably won't particularly want to work with changers much, though. SF0 might not be so lucky, and in any case, much like ItX, their infrastructure dependence is going to limit their projection capacity, which, considering they're already overextended, means that a lot of them will probably die very quickly..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T16:00:00-08:00","id":1174140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1173919#post1173919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a pretty amusing scene, but aren't Ratkin way too crazy to consider something that relatively complex and abstract?<br /> <br /> And really, why bother when the panic from a global pandemic will crash the economy and achieve the number one goal of population reduction at the same time.<br /> <br /> Manipulating the economy by itself will atract attention they don't want, while not achieving the desired megadeaths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Madness doesn't hinder the ability to go for something complex or abstract. Quite the contrary, precisely for being crazy, they are likely to develop a lot of highly abstract and unnecessarily complex plans to do anything they want done. This is probably the reason they are not far more effective already on culling humanity.<br /> <br /> On numbers I won't say much. The books never stated how many Ratkin are out there precisely, just that they are more numerous than almost any other changer, with the possible exception of the Ananasi, for similar reasons: they keep out of sight, and their animal Kin are numerous, breed in great numbers, hide easily and thrived on the modern world, dominating &quot;civilized&quot; areas even in their savage states. If the proposed scenario demands a million Ratkins on total, it is still in the acceptable spectrum.<br /> <br /> Now, let's see:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Garou</b></u><br /> Some Garou could get a hint of what is going on before it is too late. Mainly the Bone Gnawers, but also the Glass Walkers tribe would have a reasonable chance at it, along with some of the more urban members of other tribes. With their works, the Children of Gaia would be at a good place to get what is going on, while the Blood Talons would be the last to know anything without being directly informed by the Ratkin.<br /> <br /> The more Garou get on the know sooner, the more probable it is for the Nation to act more or less unified against the Ratkin on such a plan. But if information is spread in a more fractured manner, things could go far away from this. The Glass Walkers are the less likely to work with the Ratkin, but some could still see some benefit on guiding more surgical strikes with such bioweapons and still give the thumbs up. Among most of the other tribes there are still groups that would either embrace this as a return to Impergium, or accept it if their favored kinfolk are spared. Bone Gnawers can get on board for survival, Silver Fangs can want a world in turmoil to restore aristocracy, Black Furies can accept the death of men for a world of female supremacy, Silent Striders can want to exterminate the Followers of Set through any means. It is unlikely that all those scenarios happen at once, or at least in concert, and it wouldn't include all of a tribe, but just the members that are interested enough in the promised gains. Blood Talons would just collectively hide the Ratkins plans once they are sure that the diseases aren't going to kill wolves.<br /> <br /> Getting on it soon, the Nation would probably include the Ratkin in their list of Wyrm-Tainted-by-Default enemies and hunt their nests. The less visible the threat is, the more it will take a political toll for its similarity with Yet-Another-War-of-Rage. Too soon, the best moment for the Garou to act, the war would be mostly fought on propaganda and intelligence, wins the side that better convinces the bulk of the Nation. The later, the more open and desperate the war would be, and the more fractured the Nation would be as both the threat becomes more desperate and the potential to have individual agendas furthered by such extreme scenario would increase. Children of Gaia and Glass Walkers would be probably focused on developing cures and other countermeasures, while the rest would depend a lot on what is going on and who's in charge.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Nagah</b></u><br /> It depends not only on when they learn about it, but also on their actual total resources to deal with it. Such a grandiose plan would require the efforts of all the Nagah to concentrate on the Ratkins. They can achieve to keep the Ratkins at bay through enough assassination, but that would require the Nagah to go all out and have enough resources. Even at the best-case scenario, they would make their presence clear enough to other changers. At the worst-case, they would need to not only make their presence known, but actually act as diplomats to get the resources of the other changers on their side. The only way for the Nagah to not have to show themselves is for them to see ways of putting other changers on the hunt for the Ratkins.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ananasi</b></u><br /> It isn't easy to imagine how Queen Ananasa would react, but that could bring the conflict to another level. Depending on how you play the Ananasi, they can be as numerous as the Ratkin, or even more. They serve a purpose similar to that of other changers as a whole, but by their own means and mentality. They can hear to pleas from anyone, and they can ignore anyone without apparent reason. Collectively they follow only one leader, the alien mind of Ananasa, while individually they are extremely fractured already and seem to deal well with this.<br /> <br /> And they supposedly did the War-of-Rage thing with far more efficacy and less guilty than the Garou. So their response will be unpredictable, and probably different for each Spider. But if they go for it collectively, they can be the deciding force on the field, be it by killing the rats, the other changers, the humans, or just manipulating people seemingly at random.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Rokea</b></u><br /> Probably won't even notice something wrong. And when they notice, they will likely gather in numbers on the coastline just to munch on anything that falls. They want humanity dead, but they also want the Ratkin dead.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Changers</b></u><br /> On a more general take, the other changers would act depending on how much they know about what is going on. At first, they would let the Ratkins be, or otherwise deal with them as they already did. Ratkins trying to kill humans are not a novelty. But most changers are still linked enough to humanity to still care, specially when their Kinfolk is threatened. Differently from Rokea, Ratkin and Ananasi, other changers can't simply ignore their human Kin, even when they have a healthy source of animal Kin. Most still have a lot invested in human society, but not enough to have the precise planning of the Glass Walkers. And there is simply the interests, goals and problems that won't be solved by killing humanity. They mostly have less of a reason to want such a thing in the first place, at most they would want to get rid of human presence at some locations. So they are likely to invest a good deal of resources in stopping the Wererats.<br /> <br /> But at the same time, most changers don't depend on the human society enough to put it all on the fight. Wyrm-Taint generated by such a slaughter can be a serious concern, but otherwise they can still try to rebuild by themselves on the ruins of human civilization. The Garou are warriors, and even if they don't go all out they still go war-style, but other Fera not so much. They will try for it while they think it is doable, but would retreat once they think they can't stop the rats, so they can keep going without civilization.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Technocracy</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><b>Traditions</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><b>Camarilla</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><b>Sabat</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><b>Inconnu</b></u><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T16:14:30-08:00","id":1174144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1174113#post1174113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">likely while firing old surplus support weapons and AKs at their targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which are not going to have much effect against hard suits and h.i.t. marks. I think ItX stands the greatest chance of success, to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T18:55:42-08:00","id":1174183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1174144#post1174144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which are not going to have much effect against hard suits and h.i.t. marks. I think ItX stands the greatest chance of success, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about ItX hardware that's honestly just barely beyond modern armor, not BattleTech magical space armor that can stop nukes at tinfoil thickness. It's also really easy to get penetrating hits on presumably electronic hardsuits and HIT Marks when Gifts have rendered them immobile, even without a +4 to Dexterity.<br /> <br /> (for reference, rockets and recoilless rifle shells are going to be doing 10-15 base damage, which outstrips HIT Mark 5 soak, and firing full auto directly into one is likely to even things out for assault rifles.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T06:21:56-08:00","id":1174257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1174183#post1174183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not BattleTech magical space armor that can stop nukes at tinfoil thickness. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Not saying they are, but I thought the latter H.I.T. Marks were a bit more technologically advanced than &quot;barely beyond modern armor.&quot;<br /> <br /> But hey, I'll acquiesce to your expertise with Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T09:43:33-08:00","id":1174297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1174257#post1174257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not saying they are, but I thought the latter H.I.T. Marks were a bit more technologically advanced than &quot;barely beyond modern armor.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;technology&quot; was increased, but mostly to make them more subtle. Marks are supposed to be able to pass as humans, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also really easy to get penetrating hits on presumably electronic hardsuits and HIT Marks when Gifts have rendered them immobile, even without a +4 to Dexterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, let's say that countermagick doesn't work, since it's so not prepared for crossover based huge dicepools, but within that rule-loving perspective the Technocracy it's fully allowed to use ritual Magick(tm) from a safe place to eradicate all Ratkin and repopulate the planet.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if pondering about ALL the rule-lawyering that Mage can/may bring on the table would be desirable <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr />Ignoring such mechanical stuff, however, one important detail for a crossover with Mage it's the importance of mage-sight, fate, and Time based senses. The rise of Technocracy in the future was what caused Traditions to form after all-similar portents should, by all means, signal a Ratkin based apocalipse.<br /> <br /> Mages tend to react to danger beforehand. <i>Which by no means imply that they will react in a useful fashion</i>-Time would reveal that massive deaths are going to be caused by something related to rats and sickness. Most Mages don't know enough about Changers to understand this could be Ratkin's doing before their reveal themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>The Technocracy </b>would likely blame the Traditions. After all, everyone knows the Traditions want to bring back the dark ages, and what better way than with a massive plague?-it's a classic. Nephandy are likely suspect too. Best case scenario, they would try to investigate seriously, and not do anything stupid.<br /> <br /> Eventually they will understand the plague's nature, but it will be too late.<br /> <br /> <b>The Traditions </b>, as always, would be divided.<br /> Some mages will have both the will to fight and enough spiritual accumen to understand the treath. Others may ponder that this would erode both the belief in Technocratic Paradigm and their power base...and happily retire to Horizon with their loved ones to watch the show. Others will fight for their people/community with little care for the majority of human population.<br /> Some will believe that the Technocracy it's to be blamed because they're souless and mean, most will believe the cause are Nephandy.<br /> <br /> <b>Nephandi </b>would be OK with it. Destroying the world requires more than eradicating most humans, however a massive plague has it's uses: It increases the power of Banes, and thus Wyrm Nephandy would be thankful. It generates desperation, hopeless people would be easier to intruduce to the Dark Lords-Of particular interest are those Mages unable to save their loved ones from these spirit empowered sicknesses, It would be easy to sell the dark side of the force if you can produce the cure.<br /> <br /> <b>Crafts</b> These are going to protect their people, creating small places where the plagues may be resisted, they don't have the power to do much more even if they wanted to. If the Disparate aliance it's strong enough, these would be the most likely to actually form a common front against the plague, and to try to manipulate the Traditions into helping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-08-2018, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T13:31:49-08:00","id":1174352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1174297#post1174297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, let's say that countermagick doesn't work, since it's so not prepared for crossover based huge dicepools, but within that rule-loving perspective the Technocracy it's fully allowed to use ritual Magick(tm) from a safe place to eradicate all Ratkin and repopulate the planet.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if pondering about ALL the rule-lawyering that Mage can/may bring on the table would be desirable <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, all of their reality zones would have crumbled and left them in no condition to do this. Also, it's not that the countermagick outright wouldn't work, but that it just doesn't work well enough, even with the double success ratio. The Technocracy basically hoisted their own petards by making sure that huge amounts of armaments were floating around, outpacing their ability to control such threats when they lose their cutting edge shit, or when Murphy's Law started to weigh the Union's armed forces down.<br /> <br /> Ratkin would probably ease off of most engagements, though. Even Twitchers are likely to search and bomb first, before trying front line fighting. If Technocracy forces were out, about, and looking for trouble, they'd probably find a lot of Garou and W:tA antagonists before they found the Ratkin. Possibly if they tried venturing underground, they might run into a nest, but they also might run into traps laid by Engineers. Very, very simply affairs of Blasts Within a Confined Space. Anyone for chunky salsa?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T10:49:32-08:00","id":1174588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, all of their reality zones would have crumbled and left them in no condition to do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, that's not true and ultimately pointless:<br /> <br /> Untrue because, if there's no humans, there's no Consensus believing in impossibilities and causing Paradox (except for the Foundations)-also if there are humans they likely didn't stop believing in nukes and big weapons just because medicine didn't work out - apocaliptic scenarios usually believe in firepower. Hence, they won't loose most of &quot;their cutting edge shit&quot;, on the contrary, they may find easier to use it.<br /> <br /> Pointless because many of those weapons were Vulgar anyways and Paradox, RAW, it's hardly as dangerous as it's supposed to be. It could be worth a few dox points to bombard the sewers with those death rays if you have the advantage of knowing exactly where all the wererats are because one dude with Corr 3/DimSci 1/Life 1 can detect all werecreatures in the city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it's not that the countermagick outright wouldn't work, but that it just doesn't work well enough, even with the double success ratio. </div> </div> </div>Well, it's the same. Countermagick it's based on countering something that has 1/2 the dicepool of the average splat and that requires more than one successes to achieve a degree of effectivity. That's why it's more difficult that most spells, you don't need as many successes as the other mage to defend effectively. Mage it's written in such a way that this makes perfect sense - not so much elsewhere. If you double the success ratio it's more just, even if it's not the perfect fix.<br /> <br /> And if you had read what Phil stated in facebook about Primium vs Werewolves back when M20 wasn't yet released, you would know that he thinks that it would be very effective against the stop technology thing - which probably means he wasn't aware of how Gifts work.<br /> <br /> But whatever, my point was that it's somewhat unjust to think &quot;ja ja, one swap of my level 2 Gift and Technocrats are useless&quot; - if Technocrats were intended to be used like that then any Forces 2/Matter 2 mage would be invincible to them. The only reason of why such a strategy it's OP for werethings while it isn't for mages it's that their dice work different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Possibly if they tried venturing underground, they might run into a nest, but they also might run into traps laid by Engineers. </div> </div> </div>Even at their stupidest, Engineers would lay their traps in a way they don't interfere with humans (at the very least, not with their own troops), but I agree with the rest. Most likely it's that they would not discover the source of the problem until it's too late.<br /> <br /> It's worth to note-since you mention the VE-that they do have a metodology of &quot;sewer explorers&quot; that probably know more than any other tech-head about the rats. If any Technocrat it's going to have a clue about all the issue, it's going to be them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-09-2018, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T11:43:51-08:00","id":1174604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1174588#post1174588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, that's not true and ultimately pointless:<br /> <br /> Untrue because, if there's no humans, there's no Consensus believing in impossibilities and causing Paradox (except for the Foundations)-also if there are humans they likely didn't stop believing in nukes and big weapons just because medicine didn't work out - apocaliptic scenarios usually believe in firepower. Hence, they won't loose most of &quot;their cutting edge shit&quot;, on the contrary, they may find easier to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was assuming that there would be a massive breakdown in order with more targets than the Union knew how to deal with. Fomori in the streets, Chulorviah emerging from the shores in staggering numbers, Thunderwyrms stirring in the West, entities strongly resembling MIBs but who definitely weren't built by the Union, a likely Tempest in the underworld from all of the contagion-dead... no one's going to notice the rats in that shitstorm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pointless because many of those weapons were Vulgar anyways and Paradox, RAW, it's hardly as dangerous as it's supposed to be. It could be worth a few dox points to bombard the sewers with those death rays if you have the advantage of knowing exactly where all the wererats are because one dude with Corr 3/DimSci 1/Life 1 can detect all werecreatures in the city. </div> </div> </div>It might run into some difficulty being the supported action with the above going on, and possibly also interference with the &quot;dimensional energies&quot; running amok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, it's the same. Countermagick it's based on countering something that has 1/2 the dicepool of the average splat and that requires more than one successes to achieve a degree of effectivity. That's why it's more difficult that most spells, you don't need as many successes as the other mage to defend effectively. Mage it's written in such a way that this makes perfect sense - not so much elsewhere. If you double the success ratio it's more just, even if it's not the perfect fix.<br /> <br /> And if you had read what Phil stated in facebook about Primium vs Werewolves back when M20 wasn't yet released, you would know that he thinks that it would be very effective against the stop technology thing - which probably means he wasn't aware of how Gifts work. </div> </div> </div>He may have thought it, but it apparently never crossed his mind to write it into a rulebook, where it should be if we're to take it as the default shape of things. Also, if I recall that conversation correctly (just went back to look at it again on FB), he had a much softer line on it, saying that it probably wouldn't work because of the 4 dice of countermagick (assuming it was him on the M20 facebook account). The only people saying that it wouldn't work at all in that post were in no position of authority to make it so in a rulebook, and didn't even know which level JT actually was or that there were other Gifts for screwing with technology.<br /> <br /> (Speaking personally, I'd strip out any notes about Paradox or Magick and just make everything that the Technocracy uses Devices, possibly going up to 10, but Devices nonetheless. In lieu of Paradox, it would have maintenance requirements handled like various Artifacts in Exalted second edition. Make your roll, spend time and resources, restore functionality. Ultimately a trivial note that's as authoritative as the &quot;Primium shuts down everything!&quot; guy on FB.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But whatever, my point was that it's somewhat unjust to think &quot;ja ja, one swap of my level 2 Gift and Technocrats are useless&quot; - if Technocrats were intended to be used like that then any Forces 2/Matter 2 mage would be invincible to them. The only reason of why such a strategy it's OP for werethings while it isn't for mages it's that their dice work different. </div> </div> </div>Well, not quite. JT and company are spiritual effects that work through what the Technocracy would likely consider some kind of &quot;back door&quot; to reality, because Gifts only work through the world being animistic. Mages wouldn't be able to tap into that without Spirit, and I'd argue that it would be more vulgar when a mage does it, because humans like mages aren't supposed to be able to do it, in normal Mage play, or in Werewolf. If two sets of metaphysical principles that normally don't agree align against you, it's probably not going to be a good day for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even at their stupidest, Engineers would lay their traps in a way they don't interfere with humans (at the very least, not with their own troops), but I agree with the rest. Most likely it's that they would not discover the source of the problem until it's too late.<br /> <br /> It's worth to note-since you mention the VE-that they do have a metodology of &quot;sewer explorers&quot; that probably know more than any other tech-head about the rats. If any Technocrat it's going to have a clue about all the issue, it's going to be them. </div> </div> </div>Actually, I didn't mention the VE. I mentioned the Ratkin Freak Aspect, the Engineers, which, if they are present in a colony, will be responsible for its passive defenses. My apologies for not being clearer; I didn't consider the word as shorthand for the VEs at the time. As such, they will be putting traps in places that can take out TU troops, and they'll be insanely destructive ones, given the general bent of the Aspect. Which can also fire death rays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T15:40:59-08:00","id":1174679,"title":"","content":"If the Ratkin could modify the birthing plague to be semi-infectious to vampires (I'm pretty sure Black death made vampires carriers, so it's possible) then a modern city would be pretty stuffed.<br /> Follow the Herd of important vampires to infect them, or even just rats to start the Nosferatu as carriers; and it would probably increase transmission rates in a vector that CDC/mages wouldn't be able to expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T22:18:03-08:00","id":1174774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1174679#post1174679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Ratkin could modify the birthing plague to be semi-infectious to vampires (I'm pretty sure Black death made vampires carriers, so it's possible) then a modern city would be pretty stuffed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Birthing Plague is spiritual in nature, so it probably wouldn't really readily affect vampires, which are dead inside by Werewolf's figuring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Follow the Herd of important vampires to infect them, or even just rats to start the Nosferatu as carriers; and it would probably increase transmission rates in a vector that CDC/mages wouldn't be able to expect. </div> </div> </div>That would take performing a rather obvious rite every time you wanted to do it. Better to just hit them with a new strain of influenza or ebola. Those already work quite well against the vampires' deathlihood, in that the herd will be gone and the vampires will either die for good or go to sleep, where they will be easy targets for Demo-Rats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T01:36:53-08:00","id":1175939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1174774#post1174774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better to just hit them with a new strain of influenza or ebola.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't ebola make much more sense than influenza? It's blood borne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T12:16:06-08:00","id":1176019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1173152-ratkin-uprising-apocalypse-now?p=1175939#post1175939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't ebola make much more sense than influenza? It's blood borne.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DSCGoefBO7Q\" target=\"_blank\">I don't think that Plague Lords need to choose.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}